    {
      "id": "rabbi-dov-pikelny",
      "name": "Rabbi Dov B. Pikelny",
      "types": [
        "past_rabbi"
      ],
      "introduction": "Served Congregation Tifereth Israel from 1982 to 2001. The congregation honored Rabbi Pikelny and Cantor Barbara Pikelny for thirteen years of service in October 1994.",
      "biography": "Rabbi Dov B. Pikelny served Congregation Tifereth Israel from 1982 to 2001, according to the Jewish Journal's October 11, 2012 history of the congregation.\n\nIn October 1994, CTI honored Rabbi Dov B. Pikelny and Barbara Pikelny, who served as cantor, for thirteen years of involvement with the synagogue. Contemporary photographs and articles documenting the celebration are preserved in CTI archive records CTI-003, CTI-009, and CTI-038.\n\nAn obituary published in the Chicago Tribune on May 11, 2001, reports that Rabbi Pikelny, late of Marblehead, Massachusetts, died on May 9, 2001. He was the husband of the late Barbara Bromberg Pikelny, brother of Shoshana Pikelny-Goldschlag of Southfield, Michigan, and brother of the late Eli S. Pikelny. He was also survived by several nieces and nephews. Source: Chicago Tribune, May 11, 2001 (obituary excerpt supplied by CTI).",
      "photo": "assets/images/gallery/cti-1994-pikelny-recognition.jpg",
